# Commits that changed formatting only, and should not own a line in `git blame`.
#
# Enable it once per clone (GitHub honours the file automatically):
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Add a commit here ONLY if it is pure whitespace/formatting across many files.
# One full 40-character SHA per line, with a `#` comment above it naming what it
# was. A commit that mixes a real change with reformatting must not be listed --
# ignoring it would hide the real change too, which is the other half of why
# CLAUDE.md says to split those into a `format:` commit and a change commit.
#
# The C++ conversion is deliberately incremental (format the file you touch, in
# the commit that touches it), so this file is expected to stay empty. It exists
# so that a future dedicated cleanup pass -- `check_cpp.py --report --fix`, which
# rewrites the whole tree -- has somewhere obvious to record itself instead of
# destroying blame for every source file.
